# Test: ze doctor reports a kernel capability a configured subsystem needs
# Spec: plan/immediate/spec-kernel-capability-gate.md AC-2
# VALIDATES: a config that installs an IPsec Security Association, on a host
# whose kernel holds no XFRM dataplane, produces doctor-ipsec-xfrm-unavailable at
# ERROR severity, and the message names the subsystem, the kernel feature and the
# configuration that required it. `ze doctor` exits 1 on it, so readiness is
# false rather than merely noisy.
# PREVENTS: the failure the whole enrolment exists for. Every other IPsec surface
# reports what the engine believed at install time, so a host that cannot carry a
# single SA shows a tunnel as up and carries nothing.
#
# The probe is FORCED so the diagnostic is reached on a host whose kernel is
# healthy. Without the override this test would pass only where XFRM happens to
# be absent, which is the vacuity trap of ai/rules/interop-and-goal-validation.md.
# The XFRM kernel capability enrols on Linux ONLY: internal/component/ike/engine/kernelcap_linux.go
# carries the registration behind //go:build linux, because XFRM is a Linux
# dataplane and off Linux ze installs none. So `ze doctor` on darwin emits no
# xfrm diagnostic at all and nothing here can be reached, whatever
# ze.test.kernelcap.xfrm is forced to.
#
# This file passed on darwin until 2026-09-14 only because every stream
# assertion was checked against the whole test's output: its own
# `ze explain <code>` step printed the code its `ze doctor` step was supposed
# to produce. Per-command scoping ended that, and the honest answer is that the
# behaviour is Linux-only.
option=needs-linux

option=env:var=ze.test.kernelcap.xfrm:value=absent

tmpfs=ipsec-capability.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
vpn {
    ipsec {
        interface lo
        ike-group IKE-1 {
            proposal 1 {
                encryption aes256gcm
                hash sha256
                dh-group 14
            }
        }
        esp-group ESP-1 {
            proposal 1 {
                encryption aes256gcm
            }
        }
        site-to-site {
            peer branch {
                connection-type respond
                remote-address 203.0.113.7
                ike-group IKE-1
                esp-group ESP-1
                authentication {
                    mode pre-shared-secret
                    pre-shared-secret correct-horse-battery-staple
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json ipsec-capability.conf
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-ipsec-xfrm-unavailable
expect=stdout:contains=CONFIG_XFRM_USER
expect=stdout:contains=vpn ipsec
# The forced answer must reach the operator. A message that says the dataplane is
# missing and nothing about why names no action.
expect=stdout:contains=ze.test.kernelcap.xfrm

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze explain doctor-ipsec-xfrm-unavailable
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=CONFIG_INET_ESP
